Package: helpbuoy-relay
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Maurits van der Schee <maurits@vdschee.nl>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: systemd | systemd-standalone-sysusers
Conflicts: hmw-relay
Replaces: hmw-relay
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/mevdschee/helpbuoy
Description: relay for helpbuoy self-hosted remote support
 helpbuoy-relay is the SSH relay of HelpBuoy. Support agents (helpbuoy-desk) and the
 people they help (helpbuoy.exe on Windows) connect to it on one port;
 it authenticates their keys and splices their sessions. The screen and
 input run end to end over an inner SSH connection the relay can't read.
 .
 This package runs the relay as a hardened systemd service under its own
 system user, with its state in /var/lib/helpbuoy-relay. Manage agents and
 clients with helpbuoy-relayctl.
